From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:18:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: test_recompile_insn uses cls as its unliftable
 instruction (#16)

Remill patch 0010 lifts the register form of ccmn, so the test that expects
a LiftError for it fails with that patch. cls has no semantics with or
without 0010, and ccmn is checked against Unicorn in test_aot_simd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The test expected a LiftError for the register form of ccmn, which Remill patch 0010 now lifts
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#16

---
 dm/tools/tests/test_recompile_insn.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_recompile_insn.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_recompile_insn.py
index 454f2ccb..88fb402a 100644
--- a/dm/tools/tests/test_recompile_insn.py
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_recompile_insn.py
@@ -34,7 +34,8 @@ INSNS = [  # (word, expected disassembly)
 
 # Remill (commit 56918a8) has no semantics for these: its lifted code calls __remill_error. The translator must stop on them, naming the instruction (LiftError), never run what it did not translate.
 # adc and adcs were here too until the fork's Remill patch (fork en cours/remill-patches/0001-aarch64-add-adc-adcs.patch) gave Remill their semantics and decoders
-UNSUPPORTED = [(ccmp(0xBA400000, 'hi', 0), 'ccmn x0, x1, #0, hi'), (ccmp(0x3A400000, 'vs', 15), 'ccmn w0, w1, #0xf, vs')]
+# ccmn in its register form was here until fork Remill patch 0010 gave it semantics (test_aot_simd checks it against Unicorn): cls is the unliftable instruction now
+UNSUPPORTED = [(0xDAC01402, 'cls x2, x0'), (0x5AC01402, 'cls w2, w0')]
 
 
 def build_lib(word, tmp):
